Third-party content and separately licensed material
----------------------------------------------------

SNOMED CT
  This repository contains NO SNOMED CT content. The platform resolves SNOMED CT
  concepts at runtime from a FHIR terminology server (Ontoserver) and stores only
  the identifiers and designations required to operate the catalogue.

  SNOMED CT is distributed by SNOMED International and, in Australia, by the
  National Clinical Terminology Service (NCTS) as SNOMED CT-AU. Use of SNOMED CT
  requires an appropriate licence from those bodies. The Apache-2.0 licence covering
  this software grants no rights whatsoever to SNOMED CT content.

  Test fixtures in this repository that reference SNOMED CT identifiers do so as
  bare identifiers for validation purposes and do not redistribute SNOMED CT content.

SPIA Requesting terminology
  The Standardised Pathology Informatics in Australia (SPIA) Requesting terminology
  is maintained and published by the Royal College of Pathologists of Australasia
  Quality Assurance Programs (RCPA-QAP) and is subject to RCPA copyright. This
  repository contains no SPIA catalogue content. Any sample or fixture data derived
  from the published workbook is used with RCPA-QAP's knowledge for the purpose of
  building the platform that maintains it.

Third-party dependencies
  Runtime and build dependencies are declared in the lock files under backend/,
  transform/ and frontend/ and retain their own licences. No third-party source is
  vendored into this repository.
